// A **built-in** trait is not a local trait for anybody: it belongs to no package, so it can never
// be the side that makes an impl legal. Package `glue` therefore has to own the TYPE to implement
// `Clone` for it — and it does not.
// (This file sits at `glue/impls.noe`, so its module path derives as `glue.impls`.)

use b.thing.{Thing};

impl Clone for Thing {}
